<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Percy family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Percy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Percy family were a powerful English noble house in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a>, Earls of Northumberland from 1377. Henry Percy, Earl of Northumberland, and his son Harry Hotspur helped Henry IV to the throne, then rebelled against him, joining <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a> and Edmund Mortimer; Hotspur was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrewsbury">Shrewsbury</a> in 1403. The family remained leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> of the north for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/percy-family.jpg" alt="Percy family" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wikimandia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modern_arms_of_Percy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
